      "duration_ms": 10500,
      "caption": "fork uses a separate address space; vfork temporarily shares one.",
      "narration": "Fork gives the child a separate address space, usually using copy on write. Vfork shares memory and suspends the calling parent thread until exec or exit.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "title",
          "text": "Copy or share?",
          "x": 8,
          "y": 5,
          "w": 84,
          "h": 12,
